  "body": "> The [code unit substring](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-unit-substring-to-the-end-of-the-string) from index start to the end of a string string is the [code unit substring](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-unit-substring-by-indices) from start to string’s length − 1 inclusive within string.\r\n\r\nFor example, given the empty string, the result of\r\n“the [code unit substring](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-unit-substring-to-the-end-of-the-string) from index 0 to the end of the empty string”\r\nshould be the empty string, but by definition, which is:\r\n“the [code unit substring](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-unit-substring-by-indices) from 0 to − 1 inclusive within the empty string”,\r\nwihch is by definition:\r\n“the [code unit substring](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-unit-substring) from 0 with length − 1 within the empty string”,\r\nviolating the assertion \"start and length are nonnegative\".\r\n\r\nI think there is a confusion in the use of the term “indices” that the “indices” in\r\n“The [code unit substring](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-unit-substring-by-indices) from indices start to end inclusive”\r\nmeans indices between characters, while the other indices mean character position itself.\r\n\r\n",
